What, you don't memorize DEC/Compaq part numbers in your spare time? ;)  It's a

QLogic ISP1040B chip, wired for UltraWide support.  The CA variant (aka CX) is

single ended, the CB (aka CY) is differential.  You can also tell the difference

visually by the row of resistors on the CB/CY variant.  (Doesn't help in email,

tho' does it ;)

 - Pete

